sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Turing RD claim for Holstein coat spotting (tested negative hypothesis) faithfully reproduces Bos taurus (Holstein-Friesian, 10 specimens) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/1981-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Bos taurus (Holstein-Friesian, 10 specimens) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/1981-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/1981-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength.py; output: datasets/bos_taurus_turing_wavelength/bos_taurus_turing_wavelength_comparison.png; organism: Bos taurus (Holstein-Friesian, 10 specimens); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Murray (1981) proposed a reaction-diffusion pre-pattern mechanism for mammalian coat markings; Turing (1952) supplied the instability theory. Neither paper measured Holstein coat patterns against the mechanism. | Established cattle genetics: KIT/MITF regulatory variants cause Holstein white spotting (Jivanji et al. 2019 GWAS; Jivanji et al. 2025 causal variants confirmed in edited mice), and mammalian melanoblast colonisation is stochastic migration plus proliferation (Mort et al. 2016).; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg-kinetics RD (not Murray's own kinetics) on static and growing domains with gamma heterogeneity, compared with an Eden-process melanoblast-colonisation control, on 10 coat-masked Holstein specimens at matched measurement scale with paired Wilcoxon/bootstrap statistics (Pass 8). | Published result is negative: static Turing rejected (6.46 vs ~3.3); growing RD vs colonisation indistinguishable (3.29 vs 3.43, p = 0.91). Two blinded independent assessments (54.4, 57.7) overturned two earlier builder conclusions (Passes 4, 7-8) before this verdict was reached.; transfer_boundary: The verdict concerns Holstein-Friesian flank spotting measured by adult patch statistics. It does not transfer to other breeds, other pattern elements (e.g. fine speckling), embryonic pre-pattern stages not observable in adult coat, or other species; Turing mechanisms are experimentally established in other systems (e.g. palate rugae) and nothing here bears on them.; does_not_claim: Does NOT claim the Murray/Turing hypothesis is supported -- the tested claim is reported as a negative result, and the rubric overall (74.6) scores the simulation package, not the hypothesis. | Does NOT claim all reaction-diffusion models are excluded: a growing-domain RD is statistically indistinguishable from colonisation on these statistics, so adult coat morphology alone cannot identify the mechanism either way. | Does NOT claim the Eden control is the true mechanism; it is a minimal colonisation proxy, and its founder density was selected on specimen 01 (disclosed). | Does NOT claim independent confirmation of the Pass 8+ verdict: the Pass 9 assessment is builder-scored (independent re-score is remediation R11), held-out n = 9 specimens limits power, and coat segmentation is a saturation heuristic.]; phenomenon_size: 50 cm (0.5 m, log10=-0.301 m, tier=8_colonial_m); species_scale_ladder (2 runs from 9.5 mm to 50 cm): 9.5 mm:airway-mucosal-creasing, 50 cm:bos-taurus-turing-wavelength" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/s13258-016-0493-4>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms10288>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.adt5913>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1186/s12711-019-0506-2> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/1981-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/1981-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

